WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.040
Good Morning, Hank, and welcome to my new camcorder!

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:05.980
It's Tuesday. It's Question Tuesday, the day that I answer real questions from real nerdfighters.

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:09.660
"How long has the Project for Awesome been going on?" This will be the third year.

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:14.320
"How do I get my girlfriend to love me more than Jacob Black?" Ok, the first thing you wanna do is you wanna

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:21.720
see if your torso can be contorted in to V, because that's a helpful start. Then, become really hairy. But only sometimes.

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:25.020
"Wait, what is the Project for Awesome? How do I make a video and where do I post it?"

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:29.320
The Project for Awesome is an annual tradition in which lots of people make videos for charities they care about,

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:33.900
and then lots of other people rate and favorite and comment on those videos over and over and over again,

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:39.580
so that for one day, the most popular videos on youtube aren't about boobs or hamsters on piano, but about decreasing world suck.

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:43.540
If you wanna make a video, just make one advocating for your favorite charity, upload it on Thursday,

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:48.600
and ideally, find a way to make sure that the thumbnail of your video is this, which you can find at a link in the dooblydoo.

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:52.220
And then get your rating and commenting fingers ready for forty-eight hours of fun.

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:58.340
"This guy I really like wants my advice on how to ask out another girl. What should I do?" Alright, listen, this is going to sound crazy, but I

00:00:58.340 --> 00:01:03.360
have a suspicion that the guy in question actually likes you. I might be wrong about this, but

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:10.780
boys commonly have this insane strategy, wherein we tell the girl we like that we need advice on how to ask out a different girl,

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:13.560
I realize this is a colossally stupid strategy,

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:17.880
but if you look in comments, I bet you'll see a lot of guys who are like, 'yeah, I have done that.'

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:24.020
"What time should I upload my Project for Awesome video?" As close to noon Eastern time as possible, which is five pm GMT.

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:27.880
"How do I get a woman's attention to see if she likes me? We've been friends for a while,

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:33.520
so my logical thought is that I should grow a mustache. Am I far off?" See, girls, that is how we think.

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:36.940
We're like, 'maybe I should grow a mustache to get her attention'.

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:41.280
"Wait, what can I do for Project for Awesome if I can't make a video?" Okay, 90% of the Project for Awesome

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:44.740
is not in making videos, it's in commenting and rating upon videos.

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:48.940
There will be a live show that goes from Thursday at noon until Saturday morning,

00:01:48.940 --> 00:01:52.060
We're going to use that live show - by the way, there will be a link on Thursday morning - to organize,

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:58.500
to go from video to video to video, making sure that we get tons and tons of comments and ratings and favorites on each one.

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:04.480
And it will only work if there are a lot of us, so come and spend as much of your Thursday and Friday as possible

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:09.400
with Hank and me, I promise it'll be fun. If you like nerdy fun, which, let's face it, you do.

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:13.600
"How do I get my ex girlfriend back?" Read up on Buddhist non-attachment, link in the dooblydoo.

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:16.900
"How do I get the picture that I can download in the dooblydoo to be the thumbnail in my video?"

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:22.540
Unfortunately, that pretty hard. We think we've cracked YouTube's algorithm, you can find out more at projectforawesome.com.

00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:28.480
But if that doesn't work, just do your best to be creative about the thumbnail, and remember that it can be a great Project for Awesome video even without the thumbnail.

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:33.480
"You have a lot of advice about guys and girls who wanna find each other, but what about gay people?" Same advice, different pronouns.

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:38.260
"Any advice on how to make my Project for Awesome video good?" Yeah, remember that you're not just talking about a charity,

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:42.680
you're trying to advocate for that charity, so try to be as creative and awesome as possible.

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:44.940
Also, you might wanna find creative ways to encourage fundraising.

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:50.960
I, for example, will be auctioning off my one and only pair of nerd glasses, which I wore for most vlogbrothers videos in 2008.

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:54.520
"What's the best way to tell a close friend that you're in nerdfighter-like with them?"

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:59.620
I would show them this video, in fact, pause it right now, go get that person, and bring them back.

00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:05.580
Hi there, this is John Green of the vlogbrothers. You have a close friend, in nerdfighteria, who...mm... kinda likes you.

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:10.020
No big deal! Don't freak out, and don't reveal anything. Don't tell them what you're feeling yet,

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:13.480
Pokerface. P-p-p-p-p-p-p-p-pokerface.

00:03:13.480 --> 00:03:18.200
Think it through before you respond. And remember, this isn't some like some 'ohhh, I can't live without you' thing,

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:25.700
this is a 'I like you if you like me, but if you don't like me, that's cool, our friendship is wonderful and I don't wanna put it in jeopardy' thing.

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:29.280
But, y'know, if you're open to the idea, this person does think you're sort of adorable.

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:33.020
"What is the right age to start having sex?" Mmmmm... forty-two.

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:36.940
"Hey, the bookcase! Is that different from your old bookcase?" Yes, it is.

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:43.460
"Why'd you change where you film?" Oh, there were a bunch of reasons. The whole home re...holy snood, is that a crib?!?

00:03:43.460 --> 00:03:46.600
What is a crib...the Yeti's gonna have a little Yeti!!

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:48.040
Win-kitty!!!!

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:51.580
[John, offscreen] Willy, what do you think about this whole baby business?

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:53.800
[woman, offscreen] I'm concerned.

